 "notes": "Hin Muang (Purple Rock), a completely submerged ridge about 200 m by 25 m (Phuket Dive Guide) with its top at 6-8 m, three main pinnacles and several smaller ones, and walls dropping past 60 m on the south side; the whole ridge is a manta cleaning station and the currents sweep along both sides. The site coordinates (an OSM reef node at 7.3674, 98.8700) sit 24 km north-east of the real site; the origin here is placed 630 m west of Hin Daeng (the OSM offset between the two reef nodes, applied to the Hin Daeng dive-site node at 7.1490, 98.8236). Positions are approximate.",
